cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "fortocorrpy: Topographic correction of optical satellite imagery over rugged terrain"
abstract: >-
  fortocorrpy performs topographic correction of optical surface-reflectance
  imagery over rugged terrain. It implements six correction
  methods (cosine, C-correction, SCS, SCS+C, statistical-empirical, and
  empirical rotation) within a single interface, with forest masking from an
  NDVI raster or a land-cover raster and four-aspect regression balancing,
  and optionally reports reflectance-level evaluation metrics for each method
  in the same call. Correction is driven by the image grid geometry, a DEM,
  and the acquisition time; images on a common pixel lattice can be corrected
  in a single call, with the terrain data computed once and a shared forest
  source reused across them. Built on NumPy, rasterio, and pyproj.
type: software
